<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Halo was incensed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Everything he tried to salve his rage was like more oil on a fire.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Or, if not oil, petrol.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Or, if not petrol, then another three strikes of the Nightclub Vampire. Halo\'92s 
\f2\i Slice of Life
\f1\i0  was getting quite the polishing of late. But not even three more murders dissuaded the dullard Commissioner of UPI or, indeed Halo\'92s Bureau of Preemptive Reciprocity and Proactive Euthanasia (affectionately known as PAPER) from liking Tony for the Nightclub Vampire serial killings. If Halo could think of one thing worse than being caught, it would be having someone else getting the credit for his mayhem. But even worse, the ever-more incompetent authorities were holding Tony, who Halo had spent the last eight years befriending and protecting against unexplained accidents, health issues (read 
\f2\i poisonings
\f1\i0 ), mis-adventurous holidays (frayed bungee ropes) and sporting pursuits (white-water rafting in a river laced with barbed wire). Clearly the people in the know\'97and Halo was still yet to figure out who was a member of 
\f2\i that
\f1\i0  cartel\'97had sunk to framing Tony for crimes only Halo was talented enough to commit.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo was incensed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>And feeling more than a little guilty about his failure to protect Tony.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Of course, it was a matter of Halo getting complacent, or sloppy, or even more interested in picking up a target at the 
\f2\i Stickett Inn
\f1\i0 . But he had to admit, that bitch Avi Grubler (also a PAPER agent, he had learned, though he was still to learn who was handling her) had distracted him as the bomb went off. 
\f2\i I come so hard when I blow things up,
\f1\i0  she had said, thereby carelessly alerting him she intended to neutralise him after she\'92d finished. Now that Halo thought of it, he should\'92ve pumped her for more information about the bombing before he\'92d stopped her heart pumping. She might have been careless enough to admit Tony was her target. Never mind; Halo was reasonably sure anyway. Tony was by far the most valuable asset in the bar\'97until Sarah walked in, and clearly Avi had no idea about her.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah was the reason Halo was doubly incensed the authorities were framing Tony. Halo needed Tony out and about, to lead him to her. None of this was agreeable to Halo\'92s solipsistic view of life; the cognitive dissonance between the way Halo wanted the world and the way it appeared to be behaving was generating voluminous electric angst in his body, which he knew could only be discharged by striking out and breaking things.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>And so he resolved to abandon the recreation of serial-killing and turn his creativity and prodigious talents to favorite hobbies: political assassination and lawn bowls.\
\pard\pardeftab360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

