\f0 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable><!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Of the lawn bowls:\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>We should say little, as it is tangential to the consequences of Halo\'92s other pursuits. But why lawn bowls? Halo liked the shoes. And the hats. And he liked the smell of fresh-cut grass almost as much as he enjoyed the smell of fresh-cut humanity. Lawn bowls provided a rare restorative alternative to his serial-killing, unlike his previous past-time: knitting. The needles reminded him too much of stabbing, and the yarn too much of garrotting. Even knitting the fluffiest of mittens quickly spun him back to his murderous ways, while lawn bowls led to little more than the odd after-game lime-soda-and-bitters among harmless comrades and adversaries with dentures.\
\pard\pardeftab360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

